      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pittsburg%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was originally named Edwards before officially becoming Pittsburg, Oklahoma, on August 27, 1909.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pittsburg%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1910, Pittsburg boasted two railroads, a bank, a pharmacy, and several other local businesses.",
